[32m+ ### 3.4 Response Format[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ All API responses follow a consistent structure:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ```json[m
[32m+ // Success[m
[32m+ { "success": true, "data": { ... }, "message": "..." }[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ // Error[m
[32m+ { "success": false, "message": "Error description" }[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ // Validation error[m
[32m+ { "success": false, "message": "Validation failed", "errors": ["field error details"] }[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 3.5 Authentication Middleware[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ The backend uses `backend/middleware/auth.js` which exports:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ - `authenticate`: Verifies JWT, loads user from DB, checks `isActive`, attaches `req.user`[m
[32m+ - `isAdmin`: Requires `role === 'admin'` or `role === 'superadmin'`[m
[32m+ - `isSuperAdmin`: Requires `role === 'superadmin'`[m
[32m+ - `isAccredited`: Requires `isAccredited === true`[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 3.6 Internationalization (i18n)[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ The backend supports four languages: `en`, `zh`, `ms`, `ta`. Language is determined in order:[m
[32m+ 1. User's saved `language` field[m
[32m+ 2. `Accept-Language` header[m
[32m+ 3. `?lang=` query parameter[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ Translation keys use dot notation: `auth.login.success`, `tokens.create.symbol_exists`, etc.[m
