[32m+ ## 4. Developer Guide — WebSocket[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 4.1 Connection[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ The WebSocket server uses Socket.IO and runs on the same port as the HTTP server.[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ ws://localhost:3000      (development)[m
[32m+ wss://api.example.com    (production)[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 4.2 Authentication[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ Clients authenticate during the handshake:[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ```js[m
[32m+ const socket = io("ws://localhost:3000", {[m
[32m+   auth: { token: "eyJhbGc..." }[m
[32m+ });[m
[32m+ ```[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ The server verifies the JWT. If the token is invalid, the connection is rejected.[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 4.3 Events[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ | Direction | Event | Payload | Description |[m
[32m+ |-----------|-------|---------|-------------|[m
[32m+ | Client -> Server | `send-message` | `{ recipientId, content, orderId, attachments }` | Send a message |[m
[32m+ | Client -> Server | `typing` | `{ recipientId }` | Typing indicator |[m
[32m+ | Client -> Server | `mark-read` | `{ senderId }` | Mark messages as read |[m
[32m+ | Server -> Client | `new-message` | `Message` object | New message received |[m
[32m+ | Server -> Client | `message-sent` | `Message` object | Message send confirmation |[m
[32m+ | Server -> Client | `user-typing` | `{ senderId }` | Typing indicator |[m
[32m+ | Server -> Client | `messages-read` | `{ readBy }` | Messages marked as read |[m
[32m+ | Server -> Client | `error` | `{ message }` | Error event |[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 4.4 Rooms[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ Each user is automatically joined to a room named after their user ID (`socket.join(userId)`). Messages are emitted to the recipient's room.[m
[32m+ [m
