[32m+ ## 5. User Guide — How to Tokenize Assets[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 5.1 Register an Account[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ 1. Open the mobile app or use the API[m
[32m+ 2. Provide a username, email, and password (minimum 8 characters)[m
[32m+ 3. Verify your email (if verification is enabled)[m
[32m+ 4. Log in to receive your JWT token[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 5.2 Verify Your Legal Identity (ACRA)[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ For institutional tokenization (SPV-backed):[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ 1. Look up your Singapore entity by UEN[m
[32m+ 2. Submit the entity for ACRA verification[m
[32m+ 3. Once verified, your `legalIdentity` will include the entity name, status, and verification fingerprint[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 5.3 Create a Tokenization Proposal[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ 1. Provide the property address (Singapore postal code must be 6 digits)[m
[32m+ 2. Set the property type (residential, commercial, mixed, industrial)[m
[32m+ 3. Enter the valuation and currency (default SGD)[m
[32m+ 4. Configure fractionalization (total shares, decimals, issuer reserve)[m
[32m+ 5. Add registry evidence (title number, lot number, or strata lot number)[m
[32m+ 6. Set compliance requirements (offering type, accredited investor requirement)[m
[32m+ 7. Preview the fractionalization math to confirm the pricing[m
[32m+ 8. Submit the tokenization — a `Token` document is created in the database[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 5.4 Verify Registry Evidence[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ 1. Generate a registry fingerprint (SHA-256 hash of the evidence)[m
[32m+ 2. Submit the fingerprint via the verify-registry endpoint[m
[32m+ 3. The system compares the submitted fingerprint with the stored evidence[m
[32m+ 4. Verification status updates to `verified`, `rejected`, or `expired`[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 5.5 Manage Tokens[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ Once a token is active:[m
[32m+ - Investors can view the token details and prices[m
[32m+ - The admin can update the asset valuation[m
[32m+ - Token holders interact with the smart contract for transfers and governance[m
[32m+ - The admin can pause or close the offering[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ ### 5.6 Voting on Proposals[m
[32m+ [m
[32m+ If the smart contract has been deployed:[m
[32m+ 1. A token holder calls `propose()` with a description and a hash of the intended execution data[m
[32m+ 2. Other holders `castVote()` during the voting period (weight = their balance)[m
[32m+ 3. After the voting period, anyone calls `executeProposal()`[m
[32m+ 4. The proposal passes if `forVotes > againstVotes` AND total votes >= quorum[m
[32m+ [m
